knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3741
What it fixes: On a Nitro production build of a Pages Router app, `/_next/image` answered 404:
the Pages request handler only serves it through a Workers ASSETS binding, and Nitro has none.
So an image whose loader keeps the default optimizer (the built-in loader, or an
`images.loaderFile` that returns `/_next/image/?url=...` URLs, as in the Next.js deploy test
next-image-new/loader-config-default-loader-with-file) never loaded.
When there is no ASSETS binding and Nitro's app is on globalThis.__nitro__.default, the handler
now serves `/_next/image` through handleNitroImageOptimization (from the vinext-3741 patch, which
MUST apply first), exactly as the App Router handler does there; a `url` that is itself the image
optimizer is rejected with Next.js's 400. Any other path keeps returning false (Nitro serves it).
This is the Pages Router half of the #3741 port; upstream #3741 covers the App Router only. It is
a separate file so an install that already carries the App Router half still applies cleanly.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3741 with the Pages Router path covered.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

